# The gate lives in scripts/gate.sh so this hook and `npm run gate` share one
# implementation (the build-pipeline spec requires they mirror each other).
# A fail-fast prefix of cheap checks, then `vitest run` ∥ `vite build`
# concurrently, failing the commit if either fails. The steps are the commands in
# scripts/gate.sh, where each carries its reason in a comment. Deliberately
# not repeated here — this comment was one of six
# transcriptions that had drifted apart (`state-the-gate-steps-once`).
#
# Two env vars scope this run by role, and both rely on CI as the backstop:
#
#   GATE_BIOME_STAGED=1  biome checks only the staged files (a commit can only
#                        unformat a file it touches).
#   GATE_PRECOMMIT=1     a commit touching only documentation (docs/, openspec/,
#                        AGENTS.md and friends — never help/, which is a build
#                        input) skips vitest and vite build. It is also the one
#                        signal a test reads to do less here than on push
#                        (`PRECOMMIT_HOOK_RUN` and `perCommit` in
#                        engine/testing/slow.ts), so there is one name for one
#                        idea rather than a second switch to keep in step.
#
# CI and a manual `npm run gate` leave both unset and run everything, so nothing
# reaches `main` without the full gate having seen it. See scripts/gate.sh.
GATE_BIOME_STAGED=1 GATE_PRECOMMIT=1 sh scripts/gate.sh
